   "published_Date": "05/06/2026 15:32:43",
   "market_type": "Cotton Prices",
   "slug_id": 3895,
   "slug_name": "AMS_3895",
   "report_title": "Monthly Cotton Price Statistics",
   "final_ind": "Final",
   "report_narrative": "<p>****Due to the Government Shutdown, Warehouse Cotton Loan Quantities (Pg. 1) and Farm Prices (Pg. 23) are not available**** Spot cotton quotations were 174 points lower than the previous month, according to the USDA, Agricultural Marketing Service's Cotton and Tobacco Program. The average spot quotation in the seven designated markets for color 41, leaf 4, staple 34, mike 35-36 and 43-49, strength of 27.0-28.9 grams per tex, and uniformity of 81.0-81.9 units was 60.60 cents per pound in October 2025. This compares with 62.34 from the previous month. The average basis for the base quality at the end of October was 382 points off the ICE December 2025 No. 2 futures contract. Spot transactions reported in the designated markets for October totaled 40,438 running bales. bales. <strong><span style=\"color:#b60205;\">*For the correction- only the weighted monthly averages in Table 14 were updated; no other changes were made.*</span></strong></p>",
   "special_notes": "Only the weighted monthly averages in Table 14 were updated; no other changes were made."
  }
 ],
